; orpot stand holder for the net3 pot (arm A (slot from top), arm B (slot from bottom), lock disc)
; pot: 3" net cup, TYPICAL catalogue size (NOT measured): lip 80, body 72 under the lip, bottom 55, height 75. Caliper yours and pass --net-* before cutting
; material ply3: t 2.63 mm, slots drawn 2.63 mm, kerf 0.1 mm
; geometry (mm): lift 18.0, z_pot 20.63, top 91.63, reach 135.6, foot 76.04, disc_d 55.5, tongue 27.75, halflap 10.31, holes [36.7, 14.6, 13.2]
; X0 Y0 = bottom-left corner of the stock
; quickcut: GRBL diode-laser cut, static M3, warmup on every path
; cut: ply3 100% (S1000 of 1000) F350 x1; warmup 1000ms = 5.8mm
; every cut: warmup wiggle (half the warmup out and back), then the passes;
; closed loops overlap the warmup distance past their start; middle-out order
;
;HEAD: laser
;MATERIAL: ply3
;LASER_MODE: static  (M3, constant power; assumes Z already at focus)

$32=1   ; GRBL laser mode (assumes firmware $30=1000)
G21     ; mm
G90     ; absolute
M5      ; laser off

